        "title": "Contain Codex interleaved overcount and add fork provenance fixtures (#2037)",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Contain intra-file interleaved Codex cumulative counters with the file-local watermark/min-cap policy from #2066.\n- Add sanitized Issue #2037 fork-family fixtures and hand oracles (`33ce→3869`, `4d90→52bf`, and missing-parent siblings).\n- Lock ordinary parent-present `#1164` accounting with scanner integration tests.\n- Document the P0 corpus findings and canonical fork-family provenance design.\n- **Does not close #2037.** The affected Ultra reporter shape and a complete cross-file provenance ledger remain open.\n\n## Missing-parent safety decision\n- Runtime token-only sibling-prefix suppression was removed in `5441ff75`.\n- Distinct sibling events can have identical `last_token_usage` / `total_token_usage` vectors at the same ordinal. Treating those counters as event identity can silently undercount legitimate work.\n- Envelope timestamps are rewritten across copied prefixes, model is not reliably present on `token_count`, and adding more token fields only reduces collision probability. Therefore missing-parent siblings fail open: retain possible copied-prefix overcount rather than destructively suppress ambiguous rows.\n- A focused equal-counter sibling regression asserts both distinct events remain billable.\n\n## Deferred provenance work\n- Prove a copy-stable event identity stronger than token values.\n- Build cross-window family closure, collision handling, ownership migration, and the incomplete/contained quality path.\n- Add redacted initial and cached repeat-scan output from an affected real Codex setup. Sanitized fixtures and tests are supplemental evidence, not that live proof.\n\n## Relationship to #2066\n- This branch contains the #2066 file-local containment commit; the two PRs should not be merged independently as separate implementations.\n- The provenance fixtures/specs in this PR are design evidence for the later family-ledger work, not a claim that token-only cross-file dedupe is safe.\n- Neither PR uses `Fixes #2037`.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `swift test --filter Issue2037`\n- [x] `swift test --filter 'codex interleaved'`\n- [x] `swift test --filter 'codex forked child'`\n- [x] `make check`\n- [x] `make test` — 618 selections, 52/52 groups passed\n- [ ] Redacted initial + cached repeat-scan output from an affected real setup\n",
